{
  "$schema": "../../scenario.schema.json",
  "id": "tools/a-later-turn-s-request-extends-the-previous-turn-s",
  "title": "A later turn's first request opens with what the previous turn's last request sent, word for word, then its answer: every earlier round is replayed whole, however many calls came after it",
  "rules": [
    "§6.4"
  ],
  "notes": "Python: channels/_tool_history.py tool_rounds; tests/test_channels/test_tool_history.py::test_a_later_turn_s_request_extends_the_previous_turn_s. A provider that caches a prompt's prefix keeps the whole history only while each request extends the one before it (RMK-1370). Nine calls of 150 to 180 characters each: a window of the last 8 calls, the 3 most recent whole and the older ones a 120-character preview, rewrote the history at each turn. A call's arguments are left out of chat_messages: each implementation writes their JSON its own way, the same way from one turn to the next.",
